{"title": "Sectional Mock #76 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The following graph shows the population of man, woman and children in 6 different villages. The population of man, woman and children is given in thousand.</p><p><img width=576 height=336 id=\"Chart 8\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21057/image019.png\"></p><p>Difference between total population of man of village Y and Z is what percent of the difference between total population of woman of village U and V?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2352;&#2375;&#2326; 6 &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2327;&#2366;&#2306;&#2357;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306;, &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;, &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2330;&#2381;&#2330;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2332;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><p><img width=\"576\" height=\"336\" id=\"Chart 8\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21057/image019.png\"></p><p>&#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2357; Y &#2324;&#2352; Z &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352;, &#2327;&#2366;&#2305;&#2357; U &#2324;&#2352; V &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["47%", "70%", "68%", "80%"], "options_hi": ["47%", "70%", "68%", "80%"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Difference between total population of man of village Y and Z = 60  -  36 = 24</p><p>Difference between total population of woman of village U and V = 75  -  45 = 30</p><p>Required percentage = <img width=24 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21057/image020.png\"> * 100 = 80%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Difference between total population of man of village Y and Z = 60  -  36 = 24</p><p>Difference between total population of woman of village U and V = 75  -  45 = 30</p><p>Required percentage = <img width=24 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p21057/image020.png\"> * 100 = 80%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two trains of lengths 150 m and 250 m run on parallel lines. When they run in the same direction, they take 20 seconds to cross each other and, when they run in the opposite direction, they take 5 seconds to cross each other. What is the speed of the two trains?</p>", "q_hi": "150 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; 250 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2357;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2332;&#2348; &#2357;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368;&#2340; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["150 km/h and 105 km/h", "150 km/h and 250 km/h", "180 km/h and 108 km/h", "160 km/h and 106 km/h"], "options_hi": ["150 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 105 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "150 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 250 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "180 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 108 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "160 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; 106 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let speed of both trains be x m/s and y m/s respectively,</p><p>Length is given as 150 m and 250 m respectively.</p><p>When running in same direction:-</p><p>(150+250)/20=x-y</p><p>20=x-y----(i)</p><p>And when running in opposite direction:-</p><p>(150+250)/5=x+y</p><p>80=x+y---(ii)</p><p>On solving eq (i) and (ii) we get:</p><p>X=50 m/sec=50*18/5=180 km/h and</p><p>y=30 m/sec =30*18/5=108km/h.</p><p>option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let speed of both trains be x m/s and y m/s respectively,</p><p>Length is given as 150 m and 250 m respectively.</p><p>When running in same direction:-</p><p>(150+250)/20=x-y</p><p>20=x-y----(i)</p><p>And when running in opposite direction:-</p><p>(150+250)/5=x+y</p><p>80=x+y---(ii)</p><p>On solving eq (i) and (ii) we get:</p><p>X=50 m/sec=50*18/5=180 km/h and</p><p>y=30 m/sec =30*18/5=108km/h.</p><p>option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of the canvas cloth needed to erect a right conical tent of height 20 ft. and circular base of circumference 30&#960; ft. is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>20 &#2347;&#2368;&#2335; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; 30&#960; &#2347;&#2368;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2340;&#2350;&#2381;&#2348;&#2370; &#2325;&#2379; &#2326;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2325;&#2376;&#2344;&#2357;&#2366;&#2360; &#2325;&#2346;&#2337;&#2364;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["455&#960; sq.ft.", "375&#960; sq.ft.", "589&#960; sq.ft.", "470&#960; sq.ft."], "options_hi": ["455&#960; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;.", "375&#960; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;.", "589&#960; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;.", "470&#960; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2347;&#2369;&#2335;."], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>h = 20 ft</p><p>Circumference of circular base = 30&#960; ft</p><p>2 * &#960; * r = 30&#960; </p><p>r = 15 ft </p><p>l = &radic;(15<sup>2</sup> + 20<sup>2</sup>) = &radic;625 = 25 ft </p><p>Curved surface area of conical tent = &#960; * r * l = &#960; * 15 * 25 = 375&#960; sq.ft. </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>h = 20 ft</p><p>Circumference of circular base = 30&#960; ft</p><p>2 * &#960; * r = 30&#960; </p><p>r = 15 ft </p><p>l = &radic;(15<sup>2</sup> + 20<sup>2</sup>) = &radic;625 = 25 ft </p><p>Curved surface area of conical tent = &#960; * r * l = &#960; * 15 * 25 = 375&#960; sq.ft. </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many natural numbers are there between 103 and 460 which are divisible by 9?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>103 &#2324;&#2352; 460 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379; 9 &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["30", "50", "40", "45"], "options_hi": ["30", "50", "40", "45"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>First number that is divisible by 9 = 108</p><p>Last number that is divisible by 9 = 459</p><p>Difference = 9</p><p>Total number of terms or numbers between 108 and 459 = [(459  -  108)/9] + 1 = 40</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>First number that is divisible by 9 = 108</p><p>Last number that is divisible by 9 = 459</p><p>Difference = 9</p><p>Total number of terms or numbers between 108 and 459 = [(459  -  108)/9] + 1 = 40</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>&#8710;ABC has &#8736;A = 70&deg;, &#8736;B = 80&deg;. D is the incentre of &#8710;ABC. DM is perpendicular to BC and DP is the angle bisector of &#8736;BDC. Find &#8736;PDM.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#8710;ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8736;A = 70<sup>0</sup>, &#8736;B = 80<sup>0</sup> &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; D, &#8710;ABC &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2307;&#2325;&#2375;&#2344;&#2381;&#2342;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; DM, BC &#2346;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; DP, &#8736;BDC &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#8736;PDM &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["25&deg;", "12.5&deg;", "15&deg;", "7.5&deg;"], "options_hi": ["25<sup>0</sup>", "12.5<sup>0</sup>", "15<sup>0</sup>", "7.5<sup>0</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=297 height=148 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14580/image005.png\"> </p><p><img width=201 height=147 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14580/image006.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=297 height=148 id=\"Picture 9\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14580/image005.png\"> </p><p><img width=201 height=147 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p14580/image006.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B, and C together invest Rs. 57800 in a business. A invests Rs. 2500 more than B and B invests Rs. 2000 more than C. Out of a total profit of Rs. 46240, find the share of A and C together.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 57800 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; A, B &#2360;&#2375; 2500 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; B, C &#2360;&#2375; 2000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 46240 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; A &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 32560", "Rs. 28960", "Rs. 17280", "Rs. 30960"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 32560", "&#2352;&#2369;. 28960", "&#2352;&#2369;. 17280", "&#2352;&#2369;. 30960"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let C's investment be Rs. 'X'.</p><p>B's investment = X + 2000</p><p>A's investment = X + 2000 + 2500 = X + 4500</p><p>X + 2000 + X + 4500 = 57800</p><p>X = 17100</p><p>A's share: B's share: C's share = 21600: 19100: 17100 = 216: 191: 171</p><p>Hence, A and C's share = 46240 * 387/578 = Rs. 30960</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let C's investment be Rs. 'X'.</p><p>B's investment = X + 2000</p><p>A's investment = X + 2000 + 2500 = X + 4500</p><p>X + 2000 + X + 4500 = 57800</p><p>X = 17100</p><p>A's share: B's share: C's share = 21600: 19100: 17100 = 216: 191: 171</p><p>Hence, A and C's share = 46240 * 387/578 = Rs. 30960</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>30 is the mean proportional of 18 and A. Find the value of A.</p>", "q_hi": "30, 18 &#2324;&#2352; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["60", "40", "45", "50"], "options_hi": ["60", "40", "45", "50"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>18  X  A = 30<sup>2</sup></p><p>18  X  A = 900</p><p>A = 900/18</p><p>A = 50</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>18  X  A = 30<sup>2</sup></p><p>18  X  A = 900</p><p>A = 900/18</p><p>A = 50</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a race, Anurag gives a lead of 90 m to Vipul. If Anurag runs 2 times as fast as Vipul, then find the distance Anurag has to run before they meet?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;&#2327; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; 90 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;&#2327; &#2357;&#2367;&#2346;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["180 m", "200 m", "172 m", "198 m"], "options_hi": ["180 &#2350;&#2368;", "200 &#2350;&#2368;", "172 &#2350;&#2368;", "198 &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>If time of constant, then</p><p>Ratio of speed = Ratio of distance</p><p>Ratio of speed of Anurag and Vipul = 2:1</p><p>Ratio of distance = 2:1</p><p>So, </p><p>1 unit = 90 m</p><p>2 unit = 2*90 = 180 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If time of constant, then</p><p>Ratio of speed = Ratio of distance</p><p>Ratio of speed of Anurag and Vipul = 2:1</p><p>Ratio of distance = 2:1</p><p>So, </p><p>1 unit = 90 m</p><p>2 unit = 2*90 = 180 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>In an isosceles triangle JKL, JK = JL = X cm, and KL = 8 cm. From J, a median is drawn to KL that meets KL at M. If JM = 6 cm, then find the value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; JKL &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, JK = JL = X cm &#2324;&#2352; KL = 8 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; J &#2360;&#2375;, KL &#2325;&#2368; &#2323;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2326;&#2368;&#2306;&#2330;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2379; KL &#2360;&#2375; M &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; JM = 6 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["2&radic;5 cm", "&radic;13 cm", "5&radic;2 cm", "2&radic;13 cm"], "options_hi": ["2&radic;5 cm", "&radic;13 cm", "5&radic;2 cm", "2&radic;13 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><img width=223 height=191 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image037.png\"></p><p>We know that the median drawn to the base is perpendicular to the base.</p><p>And KM = KL/2 = 8/2 = 4 cm</p><p>In &#916; JKM,</p><p><img width=112 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=85 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image041.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=223 height=191 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image037.png\"></p><p>We know that the median drawn to the base is perpendicular to the base.</p><p>And KM = KL/2 = 8/2 = 4 cm</p><p>In &#916; JKM,</p><p><img width=112 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image038.png\"></p><p><img width=87 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image039.png\"></p><p><img width=60 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image040.png\"></p><p><img width=85 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23087/image041.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many times is 0.5 greater than 0.002?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>0.5, 0.002 &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["300", "200", "150", "250"], "options_hi": ["300", "200", "150", "250"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=43 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image002.png\"></p><p>= 7 + (328  -  32)/900</p><p>= 7 + 296/900</p><p>= 6596/900 = 1649/225</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=43 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28366/image002.png\"></p><p>= 7 + (328  -  32)/900</p><p>= 7 + 296/900</p><p>= 6596/900 = 1649/225</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of money deposited at simple interest amounts to Rs.1840 in 3 years and Rs.1240 in 2 years. The sum deposited is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.1840 &#2324;&#2352; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2369;.1240 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2350;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; ___ &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.40", "Rs.20", "Rs.44", "Rs.60"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.40", "&#2352;&#2369;.20", "&#2352;&#2369;.44", "&#2352;&#2369;.60"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Simple interest of 1 year = 1840  -  1240 = Rs.600</p><p>Simple interest of 2 years = 2 * 600 = Rs.1200</p><p>Sum deposited = 1240  -  1200 = Rs.40</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Simple interest of 1 year = 1840  -  1240 = Rs.600</p><p>Simple interest of 2 years = 2 * 600 = Rs.1200</p><p>Sum deposited = 1240  -  1200 = Rs.40</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 148 and ab = 54, then find the value of&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a + b", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367;  a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> = 148  &#2324;&#2352;   ab = 54, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;  &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">a + b", "options_en": ["8/&radic;10", "2/&radic;10", "8&radic;7", "5&radic;3"], "options_hi": ["8/&radic;10", "2/&radic;10", "8&radic;7", "5&radic;3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2 </sup>+ b<sup>2 </sup>+ 2ab</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = 148 + 2 * 54 </p><p>=&gt; (a + b)<sup>2</sup> = 148 + 108 = 256</p><p>(a + b) = 16</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2 </sup>+ b<sup>2</sup>  -  2ab</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = 148  -  2 * 54</p><p>=&gt; 148  -  108 </p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = 40 or 2&radic;10</p><p>(a+b)/(a-b) = 16/2&radic;10 = 8/&radic;10</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2 </sup>+ b<sup>2 </sup>+ 2ab</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(a + b)<sup>2</sup> = 148 + 2 * 54 </p><p>=&gt; (a + b)<sup>2</sup> = 148 + 108 = 256</p><p>(a + b) = 16</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2 </sup>+ b<sup>2</sup>  -  2ab</p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = 148  -  2 * 54</p><p>=&gt; 148  -  108 </p><p>(a  -  b)<sup>2</sup> = 40 or 2&radic;10</p><p>(a+b)/(a-b) = 16/2&radic;10 = 8/&radic;10</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A, B, and C start a business. A invests 30% of the total capital, B invests 40% of the remaining and C invests the rest. If the total profit at the end of a year is Rs 12000, then A's share in profit is: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; A &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2370;&#2305;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 30% &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, B &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2346;&#2370;&#2305;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 40% &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; C &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2346;&#2370;&#2305;&#2332;&#2368; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2352;&#2369;.12000 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; A &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2306;&#2358; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["Rs 4600", "Rs 3360", "Rs 3600", "Rs 5040"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 4600", "&#2352;&#2369;. 3360", "&#2352;&#2369;. 3600", "&#2352;&#2369;. 5040"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the total capital be '100' units.</p><p>Then A's capital = 30 units, B's capital = 70 * 40/100 = 28 units</p><p>C's capital = 70  -  28 = 42 units </p><p><img width=432 height=61 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23085/image003.png\"></p><p>A's share in profit = 12000 * 15/ 50 = Rs 3600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the total capital be '100' units.</p><p>Then A's capital = 30 units, B's capital = 70 * 40/100 = 28 units</p><p>C's capital = 70  -  28 = 42 units </p><p><img width=432 height=61 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p23085/image003.png\"></p><p>A's share in profit = 12000 * 15/ 50 = Rs 3600</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A hemispherical bowl of radius 6 cm recast into a cone of height 12 cm. Find the diameter of the base of the cone.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>6 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; 12 cm &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2369;&#2344;&#2307; &#2338;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["6 cm", "5 cm", "9 cm", "12 cm"], "options_hi": ["6 cm", "5 cm", "9 cm", "12 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the radius of the cone be r.</p><p>Volume of hemispherical bowl = Volume of cone</p><p>(2/3) * &#928; * r<sup>3</sup> = (1/3) * &#928; * r<sup>2</sup> * h</p><p>2 * 6 * 6 * 6 = r<sup>2</sup> * 12</p><p>r = 6 cm</p><p>Hence, diameter = 6 * 2 = 12 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the radius of the cone be r.</p><p>Volume of hemispherical bowl = Volume of cone</p><p>(2/3) * &#928; * r<sup>3</sup> = (1/3) * &#928; * r<sup>2</sup> * h</p><p>2 * 6 * 6 * 6 = r<sup>2</sup> * 12</p><p>r = 6 cm</p><p>Hence, diameter = 6 * 2 = 12 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If 27K<sup>6</sup> + 26K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0, then the positive value of [2K + (&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 27K<sup>6</sup> + 26K<sup>3</sup> - 1 = 0 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; [2K + ( <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">3", "options_en": ["8(1/3)", "9", "9(2/3)", "8"], "options_hi": ["8(1/3)", "9", "9(2/3)", "8"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>27K<sup>6</sup> + 26K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0</p><p>27K<sup>6</sup> + 27K<sup>3</sup>  -  K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0</p><p>27K<sup>3</sup>(K<sup>3</sup> + 1)  -  1 (K<sup>3</sup> + 1) = 0</p><p>(27K<sup>3</sup>  -  1) (K<sup>3</sup> + 1) = 0</p><p>27K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0 or K<sup>3</sup> + 1 = 0</p><p>27K<sup>3</sup> = 1 or K = -1</p><p>K<sup>3</sup> = 1/27</p><p>K = 1/3</p><p>Positive value of [2K + (3/K)]</p><p>= [(2/3) + 3 * 3]</p><p>= 9(2/3).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>27K<sup>6</sup> + 26K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0</p><p>27K<sup>6</sup> + 27K<sup>3</sup>  -  K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0</p><p>27K<sup>3</sup>(K<sup>3</sup> + 1)  -  1 (K<sup>3</sup> + 1) = 0</p><p>(27K<sup>3</sup>  -  1) (K<sup>3</sup> + 1) = 0</p><p>27K<sup>3</sup>  -  1 = 0 or K<sup>3</sup> + 1 = 0</p><p>27K<sup>3</sup> = 1 or K = -1</p><p>K<sup>3</sup> = 1/27</p><p>K = 1/3</p><p>Positive value of [2K + (3/K)]</p><p>= [(2/3) + 3 * 3]</p><p>= 9(2/3).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If SinA + Sin<sup>2</sup>A=1, then the value of the expression (Cos<sup>2</sup>A + Cos<sup>4</sup>A) is _________.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; SinA + Sin<sup>2</sup>A=1, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2306;&#2332;&#2325; (Cos<sup>2</sup>A + Cos<sup>4</sup>A) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344;_____&#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3/2", "1", "2", "1/2"], "options_hi": ["3/2", "1", "2", "1/2"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>SinA + Sin<sup>2</sup>A=1</p><p>SinA = 1- Sin<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>SinA = Cos<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>Cos<sup>2</sup>A + Cos<sup>4</sup>A</p><p>= Cos<sup>2</sup>A + (Cos<sup>2</sup>A)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= SinA + Sin<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>SinA + Sin<sup>2</sup>A=1</p><p>SinA = 1- Sin<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>SinA = Cos<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>Cos<sup>2</sup>A + Cos<sup>4</sup>A</p><p>= Cos<sup>2</sup>A + (Cos<sup>2</sup>A)<sup>2</sup></p><p>= SinA + Sin<sup>2</sup>A</p><p>= 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Rohini buys a Bluetooth headphone set for &#8377;1,700 from a wholesale shop and marks it at &#8377;2,000. Later on, she allows a discount of 40% on its sale. What is her loss or gain percentage (correct up to two decimal places)?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2352;&#2379;&#2361;&#2367;&#2339;&#2368; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2341;&#2379;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375; 1,700 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2381;&#2354;&#2370;&#2335;&#2370;&#2341; &#2361;&#2375;&#2337;&#2347;&#2379;&#2344; &#2360;&#2375;&#2335; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 2,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2348;&#2340;&#2366;&#2312;&#2404; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352; 40% &#2325;&#2368; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; (&#2342;&#2379; &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2366;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368;)?", "options_en": ["25.19% loss", "29.41% gain", "29.41% loss", "25.19% gain"], "options_hi": ["25.19% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "29.41% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;", "29.41% &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367;", "25.19% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price = 2000 * 60/100 = Rs. 1200</p><p>Loss percentage = (1700  -  1200)/1700 * 100 = 29.41%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price = 2000 * 60/100 = Rs. 1200</p><p>Loss percentage = (1700  -  1200)/1700 * 100 = 29.41%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If <img width=305 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image045.png\">, then find the value of x.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; <img width=305 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image045.png\">, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8", "16", "64", "32"], "options_hi": ["8", "16", "64", "32"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=305 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image045.png\"></p><p><img width=148 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image046.png\"></p><p><img width=97 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image047.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image048.png\"></p><p><img width=53 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image049.png\"></p><p><img width=45 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image050.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=305 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image045.png\"></p><p><img width=148 height=28 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image046.png\"></p><p><img width=97 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image047.png\"></p><p><img width=73 height=20 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image048.png\"></p><p><img width=53 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image049.png\"></p><p><img width=45 height=17 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27059/image050.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>The curved surface area of a cylinder and surface area of the sphere of equal radius of r cm, is X sq. cm and Y sq. cm respectively. If X = Y and then the height of cylinder is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>r cm &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; X sq. cm &#2324;&#2352; Y sq. cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X = Y &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["r", "r/2", "2r", "r/4"], "options_hi": ["r", "r/2", "2r", "r/4"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>X = Y</p><p>2 * &#960; * r * Height = 4 * &#960; * r * r</p><p>2 * Height = 4r</p><p>Height = 2r</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question,</p><p>X = Y</p><p>2 * &#960; * r * Height = 4 * &#960; * r * r</p><p>2 * Height = 4r</p><p>Height = 2r</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A seller sells goods at 15% profit and uses weight 14% less than the actual measure. Find his profit percentage.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; 15% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; 14% &#2325;&#2350; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["33.72%", "29.87%", "31.45%", "34.25%"], "options_hi": ["33.72%", "29.87%", "31.45%", "34.25%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let cost price of 1 kg of goods = &#8377;100</p><p>He uses 14% less weight i.e. he sells 860 gm instead of 1000 gm</p><p>Cost price of 860 gm of goods = &#8377;86</p><p>Selling price of 1 kg of goods = 115% of 100 = &#8377;115</p><p>Profit percentage = [(115  -  86)/86]*100 = 33.72%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let cost price of 1 kg of goods = &#8377;100</p><p>He uses 14% less weight i.e. he sells 860 gm instead of 1000 gm</p><p>Cost price of 860 gm of goods = &#8377;86</p><p>Selling price of 1 kg of goods = 115% of 100 = &#8377;115</p><p>Profit percentage = [(115  -  86)/86]*100 = 33.72%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The digit on tens place of a two-digit number is 4/3 of the digit on ones place. When the digits are interchanged, the difference between both the numbers is 18. Find the sum of the digits of the number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2311;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; 4/3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2310;&#2346;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 18 &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["14", "18", "15", "11"], "options_hi": ["14", "18", "15", "11"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the digit on ones place = 3m</p><p>Digit on tens place = 4m</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(10*4m + 3m)  -  (10*3m + 4m) = 18</p><p>43m  -  34m = 18</p><p>m = 2</p><p>So, the number = 86</p><p>Required sum = 8 + 6 = 14</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the digit on ones place = 3m</p><p>Digit on tens place = 4m</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>(10*4m + 3m)  -  (10*3m + 4m) = 18</p><p>43m  -  34m = 18</p><p>m = 2</p><p>So, the number = 86</p><p>Required sum = 8 + 6 = 14</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>A certain sum of money becomes 2.5 times of itself at simple interest in 6 years. What is the rate of interest?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; 6 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2351;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; 2.5 &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["25%", "36%", "20%", "30%"], "options_hi": ["25%", "36%", "20%", "30%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the rate of interest = R%</p><p>2.5P  -  P = P*R*6/100</p><p>R = 1.5*100/6</p><p>R = 25%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the rate of interest = R%</p><p>2.5P  -  P = P*R*6/100</p><p>R = 1.5*100/6</p><p>R = 25%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>(x/y) + (y/x) = P and (x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup>) = 0, then find the value of P. [where (x + y) &#8800; 0]</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(x/y) + (y/x) = P &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; (x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup>) = 0 &#2361;&#2376; , &#2340;&#2379; P &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; |(&#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; (x + y) &#8800; 0)</p>", "options_en": ["0", "1", "2", "3"], "options_hi": ["0", "1", "2", "3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>(x/y) + (y/x) = P</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>) = Pxy</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  Pxy = 0 ..... (1)</p><p>Now, (x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup>) = 0</p><p>=&gt; (x + y)(x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy = 0 ..... (2) [(x + y) &#8800; 0]</p><p>Compare equation (1) and (2)-</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  Pxy = x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy</p><p>=&gt; P = 1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(x/y) + (y/x) = P</p><p>(x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>) = Pxy</p><p>x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  Pxy = 0 ..... (1)</p><p>Now, (x<sup>3</sup> + y<sup>3</sup>) = 0</p><p>=&gt; (x + y)(x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy) = 0</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy = 0 ..... (2) [(x + y) &#8800; 0]</p><p>Compare equation (1) and (2)-</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  Pxy = x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>  -  xy</p><p>=&gt; P = 1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>In right-angled triangle ABC, &#8736;B = 90&#186; and angle A and angle C are acute angles. If cosecA = 2&radic;2, then find the value of sinA . cosC + cosA . sinC</p>", "q_hi": "&#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; ABC &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#8736;B = 90&#186; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; A &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; C &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cosecA = 2&radic;2, &#2340;&#2379; sinA . cosC  + cosA . sinC &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;", "options_en": ["0", "2&radic;2", "1", "&radic;2"], "options_hi": ["0", "2&radic;2", "1", "&radic;2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>We know that sin A &#183; cos C + cos A &#183; sin C = sin(A + C) (sine addition formula).</p><p>In a right triangle, A + C = 90&deg; (since B = 90&deg;).</p><p>Thus, sin(A + C) = sin 90&deg; = 1.</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>We know that sin A &#183; cos C + cos A &#183; sin C = sin(A + C) (sine addition formula).</p><p>In a right triangle, A + C = 90&deg; (since B = 90&deg;).</p><p>Thus, sin(A + C) = sin 90&deg; = 1.</p><p>Option (c) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">14356", "q_hi": "<p><span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">14356", "options_en": ["1/3", "3/5", "2/5", "3/4"], "options_hi": ["1/3", "3/5", "2/5", "3/4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}]}